<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 440,000 lbs antimony.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 440,000 lbs antimony.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center sold 440,000 pounds of antimony to Amalgamated Corp in a privately negotiated bid for an estimated provisional market value of $370,000, or 84.09 cents a lb.</p>
<p>The spot price was 87.31/90.71 cents a pound Tuesday.</p>
<p>Antimony is offered for sale on the fourth Tuesday of each month. The next offering is August 26.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1646))</p>
